//   The Zicfiss extension adds the SSE field in henvcfg. If the SSE field is set to 1, the Zicfiss
//     extension is activated in VS-mode. When the SSE field is 0, the Zicfiss extension remains
//     inactive in VS-mode, and the following rules apply when V=1:
//
// Context:
//   The rules: 32-bit Zicfiss instructions revert to Zimop, 16-bit ones to Zcmop; xwr=010 in VS-
//     stage tables is reserved; senvcfg.SSE is read-only zero; with menvcfg.SSE=1, SSAMOSWAP raises
//     virtual-instruction. vsatp and hgatp are Bare except for the VS-stage page-table case.
//
// Clarifications:
//   https://github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/issues/2424: "When henvcfg.sse is 0 and V is 1,
//     senvcfg.sse is read only zero. A read only zero CSR field cannot be written to and returns 0
//     on read by both hardware and software" (ved-rivos). So VU-mode with henvcfg.SSE=0 sees
//     senvcfg.SSE=0 whatever HS-mode wrote. https://github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/issues/2077:
//     "the following rules apply when V=1" (ved-rivos); MPRV/MPV do not affect accesses to the
