//     with Zcmop c.sspush/c.sspopchk) do nothing.
//   2. VS-mode and VU-mode ssamoswap raise virtual-instruction (xtval 0 or the instruction bits).
//   3. senvcfg.SSE read in VS-mode is 0 though HS-mode set it; VU-mode ssrdp writes 0. A VS-mode
//     clear of senvcfg.SSE does not change the bit HS-mode sees.
//   4. VS-stage xwr=010 is reserved: a VS-mode lw from such a page raises a load page fault.
//   5. henvcfg.SSE=1 (and senvcfg.SSE written again by HS-mode, as its V=1 view may be UNSPECIFIED
//     after the change): VS-mode ssrdp returns ssp, the same lw reads the page, and VS-mode reads
